@startuml states-payment
' SplitSmart - Payment lifecycle (reconciled candidate)
' Sources: data-model.md section 6.5; design.md section 7. Payments are immutable once recorded.
title SplitSmart - Payment Lifecycle

hide empty description
skinparam shadowing false

[*] --> Requested : sender submits\n(Idempotency-Key)
Requested --> RECORDED : [actor = sender; members; 0 < amount <= owed;\nnot an unconfirmed possible duplicate]\n/ insert; recordedBy, recordedAt; audit
Requested --> Refused : [validation or rule fails]\n/ error code; nothing stored
Requested --> RECORDED : [same key + same hash]\n/ return the original payment (no new row)
Refused --> [*]

state Requested : transient (inside one request/transaction)
state Refused : NOT_FOUND, PAYMENT_NOT_SENDER, PAYMENT_SELF,\nRECIPIENT_NOT_MEMBER, VALIDATION_FAILED, NOTHING_OWED,\nPAYMENT_EXCEEDS_OUTSTANDING, POSSIBLE_DUPLICATE_PAYMENT,\nIDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED
state RECORDED : immutable; counted in balances immediately
state RECORDED : identifiable as a settlement (NFR-005)
state RECORDED : edit / delete / void => not supported (OQ-6)

RECORDED --> [*]
@enduml
